TypeScript kya hai? 💙

TypeScript (TS) JavaScript ka superset hai.
Matlab TypeScript mein JavaScript ka almost saara code likh sakte ho, but TypeScript usme static type checking add karta hai.

Simple way:

JavaScript + Types = TypeScript

JavaScript mein:
let age = 23;
age = "Sania";

JavaScript ise allow kar deti hai.

TypeScript mein:

let age: number = 23;

age = "Sania"; // ❌ Error

Kyuki humne pehle hi bola hai ki age sirf number hoga.

TypeScript kyu use karte hain?

Bade projects mein code ko:

🐛 Errors jaldi find karne ke liye
🧠 Code ko samajhna easier banane ke liye
🔒 Types ko safe rakhne ke liye
👥 Team mein kaam karna easier banane ke liye
🛠️ Better autocomplete/editor support ke liye

use kiya jata hai.

JavaScript vs TypeScript
JavaScript	TypeScript
Dynamically typed	Statically typed
.js file	.ts file
Types optional nahi hote	Types specify kar sakte ho
Browser directly run karta hai	Usually JS mein compile/transpile hota hai
Small + large projects	Especially large projects mein useful
Example

JavaScript:

function add(a, b) {
    return a + b;
}

TypeScript:

function add(a: number, b: number): number {
    return a + b;
}

Yahan:

a: number
b: number

batata hai ki a aur b numbers hone chahiye.

Aur:

): number

batata hai ki function number return karega.

Tumhare liye abhi kya important hai?

Tum JavaScript abhi start kar rahi ho, toh TypeScript abhi start karne ki zarurat nahi hai.

Pehle JavaScript strong karo → DOM → events → arrays/objects → functions → async JS → APIs.

Uske baad TypeScript karna kaafi easy lagega. ❤️